# O11-CONTROL acceptance (author-owned). Every check must pass once the outcome is implemented.
# Written on main 70db15e (2.5.0), where 50 of these 66 fail by design (evidence-o11c-acceptance/main-probe.log;
# V5b re-run after a phase-1 fix that made it depend on the video actually stopping: main-probe-video.log).
# The 16 passing ones are setup checks (V7, V17, K1) and regression guards: Leave stops the video (V20), the 2.5.0
# protocol (X1-X4), MPRIS Playing with one layer audible (P3), the 2.x status line outside partial pause (P0, P7-P9),
# one room Pause/Play in popover and mini player (U3, U9), Stop on the Music row with no single-item menu (R1).
# Author-set limits awaiting a coordinator ruling: 6 s fixture connect, Cancel effective within 3 s, follow/popover
# change within 2 s, "nothing starts" observed until 2 s past the connect (see the probe docstring).
V1 listening-roomctl --help names the video command
V2 listening-roomctl starts the room's video from a URL the user gives (that video plays)
V2b ... as Watch: the room stays the same room and nothing else starts
V3 listening-roomctl shows the room's video: its name and that it plays
V4 while a video is watched, listening-roomctl status (Waybar) names it
V5 listening-roomctl stops the room's video: the player closes and the room reports no video
V5b ... and stopping it resumes nothing (Resume stays explicit)
V6 with the start verb working, a link that is not a public YouTube video is refused (non-zero exit, a message) and opens nothing
V7 (setup) Watch paused the room and the video plays
V8 MPRIS reports Playing while the video plays (something is audible)
V10 ... the room reports the video as paused
V10b ... and MPRIS then reports Paused
V9/V11 listening-roomctl pause / play pauses the video and then resumes it; Music and Ambience stay paused throughout (Play restores exactly what Pause paused)
V12/V13 MPRIS Pause / Play pauses the video and then resumes it; Music and Ambience stay paused throughout (Play restores exactly what Pause paused)
V14 MPRIS PlayPause twice pauses the video and then resumes it; Music and Ambience stay paused throughout (Play restores exactly what Pause paused)
V15 the media key (listening-hub toggle) twice pauses the video and then resumes it; Music and Ambience stay paused throughout (Play restores exactly what Pause paused)
V16 the window's room Pause then Play pauses the video and then resumes it; Music and Ambience stay paused throughout (Play restores exactly what Pause paused)
V17 (setup) the room resumed while the video plays
V18 with the room and the video playing, room Pause pauses all three and Play restores all three
V19 with no room, room transport pauses and resumes the video
V19b ... MPRIS reports the paused video as Paused, and no room is invented or started
V20 Leave stops the video: within 5 s (a Leave fade) the player is closed and no video is reported
X4 a 2.5.0 client's raw `video` start/stop request still opens and closes the video
P0 with everything playing the line is the playing line (class playing, nothing said paused)
P1 with the music paused on its own, status says "Music paused" and names the ambience still playing (Rain on glass)
P2 ... with a paused class
P3 ... and MPRIS PlaybackStatus is Playing (the ambience is audible)
P4 status --follow prints the "Music paused" line with the paused class within 2 s
P5 ... and the playing line again within 2 s once the music plays
P6 with the ambience paused on its own, status says the ambience is paused, names the music (SomaFM Drone Zone) and has the paused class
P7 a stopped layer is not reported as paused (music stopped, ambience playing: no "paused", class playing)
P8 the whole room paused keeps the 2.x paused line
P9 every status line read in this probe stays parseable and keeps the 2.x line outside partial pause and video (revised WP2 status oracle)
U1 the popover shows a tappable Music item and a tappable Ambience item
U2 ... under the room name
U3 the popover keeps one room Pause/Play besides the per-layer items
# U4-U8 were recorded on main under the probe's fallback names "(no per-layer items to tap)", the name
# used when the popover has no items; phase 2 (4574991) lists the real check names. Same checks, oracle fix.
U4 tapping Music pauses the music alone (the ambience keeps playing)
U5 ... and the Music item then shows it is paused (its look changed), the Ambience item unchanged
U6 tapping Music again plays it
U7 tapping Ambience pauses the ambience alone, and again plays it
U8 a pause made elsewhere (listening-roomctl music pause) shows on the popover line within 2 s
U9 the mini player keeps one room Pause/Play and no per-layer items
M1 in the Mix, M pauses the music alone
M2 ... and M again plays it
M3 in the Mix, A pauses the ambience alone
M4 ... and A again plays it
M5 Shift+Up with the Music row focused raises the music level, and neither the ambience level nor the room volume
M6 Shift+Down lowers it again, the same way
M7 Shift+Up with the Ambience row focused raises the ambience level alone
M8 with M working in the Mix, typing M or A in a text entry (Listen search) changes no layer
# M9 is superseded by M9-R1 (phase 2, 2026-11-22, on 4574991): criterion 4 lets the keys wait in one easy-to-merge
# list while O11-SHELL's table is not on the branch; the original prints as an uncounted SUPERSEDED line.
M9-R1 the Keyboard shortcuts list names M (music), A (ambience) and Shift+Up/Down (the focused row's level); while O11-SHELL's shortcuts dialog is not on the branch, one key list in the window or Mix module may hold them
R1 radio room: Stop is a button on the Music row, and no Mix menu holds a single item
R2 library room: Next track is a button on the Music row (not only in the ⋯ menu)
K1 (setup) the room was connecting when the Mix was opened
K2 while connecting, the Mix shows a progress indicator and Cancel
K3 ... and no other control (the sheet's close aside)
K4 Cancel abandons the attempt in the controller within 3 s: not connecting, back to idle
K5 nothing starts afterwards: past the moment the connect would have finished, no layer started and the room is still idle
K6 ... and the window no longer shows the connecting Cancel
K7 (setup) switching to another room was connecting, with Cancel shown
K8 Cancel while switching restores the previous room within 3 s: same room, same music, playing as before
K9 ... and nothing of the target starts afterwards: the previous room is still the one playing
X1 every 2.5.0 controller action still exists with the same argument types (changes are additive)
X2 ... and what ran at once in 2.5.0 still runs at once (stop, quiet, resume, transport, video stop)
X3 the snapshot keeps every 2.5.0 field
X5 the CHANGELOG records the change above 2.5.0: the video from roomctl and room transport, and partial pause in the status
